# channels.conf — one channel per line
#
# Format (pipe-delimited):
#   slug|Display Name|chno|logo_url|Group Name|source_page_url|mode|referer|bandwidth
#
# Allowed sources only (see "Source hard line" in the README):
#   - iptv-org/iptv category lists and guide data
#   - free ad-supported TV services (FAST lists)
#   - a broadcaster's own official free live stream or live page
# Never add pirate embed/restream sites, paid channels taken from third-party
# sites, DRM bypasses, or ways around token systems that protect paying customers.
#
# Fields:
#   slug         — unique channel ID (used in tvg-id)
#   name         — display name shown in the media player
#   chno         — channel number for ordering in the Channels tab
#   logo         — URL to a channel logo image (PNG recommended)
#   group        — group name for organizing channels
#   source_url   — the web page that contains or links to the m3u8 stream,
#                  OR (in literal mode) the m3u8 URL itself
#   mode         — extraction method: "iframe" (default), "direct", or "literal"
#                    iframe  = page has <iframe> → embed page has m3u8
#                    direct  = page itself contains the m3u8 URL
#                    literal = source_url IS the m3u8 URL (no scraping). Use
#                              this when the stream URL is published directly,
#                              e.g. in an iptv-org playlist or a FAST list.
#   referer      — (optional) override Referer sent when fetching the page.
#                  Some official streams only answer requests that carry
#                  their own site as the Referer.
#   bandwidth    — (optional) real stream bitrate in bits/sec (e.g. 6000000
#                  for 6 Mbps). When set, the proxy wraps the stream in a
#                  master playlist with this BANDWIDTH so Jellyfin reads the
#                  correct value instead of its ~20 Mbps default guess. Leave
#                  blank if the upstream is already a master playlist.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Example channels (replace the placeholders with your own allowed sources):
#
# A broadcaster's own live page, which embeds the official player:
# local-news|Local News|1|https://example.com/logos/local-news.png|News|https://broadcaster.example/live|iframe||4000000
#
# A stream URL taken from an iptv-org category list (for example the "news" category):
# iptv-org-news|Category List News|2|https://example.com/logos/news.png|News|https://cdn.example/news/playlist.m3u8|literal||
#
# A stream URL from a free ad-supported (FAST) list:
# fast-movies|FAST Movies|3|https://example.com/logos/movies.png|Movies|https://fast.example/movies/playlist.m3u8|literal||6000000
